 whoa  this time that the Punisher met  Wolverine and this time that Spiderman  fought alongside because I understand  that they do crossover but it's not  nearly with the same level of casualness  that you know various Avengers  characters crossover with each other or  very section main characters crossover  with each other they are very much kept  separate and when they meet up it's a  big deal and while there would be some  fun to be had in making a big deal out  of having them all meet up I just think  it's ultimately going to a completely  clutter and make the MCU almost  unmanageable and deprive us of a much  more potentially unique voice as a  contrast to what Marvel is doing with  his characters because like I said at  the beginning Marvel and Disney would  not have made Deadpool and they  definitely would not have made Logan and  that's why as much as I don't want them  to make any more bad movies I'm happy  that Fox still has this property and I  want them to keep trying I don't want  them to give up and I want them to be  sure that what they're doing is not just  trying to do the same thing that Marvel  doesn't they are  your own thing and so far pass or fail  they have been doing that so keep doing  that  give us the variety give us not  everything that feels the same and look  I understand for x-men fans that Fox has  botched some of these characters 'm some  of these stories badly and you are angry  about that and you believe that Marvel  would do it right and maybe they would  if they'd had control of these things  from the beginning but at this point the  MCU is too far along to well-established  would it have worked if Marvel had  control of x-men at the time they  started the MCU maybe it's too late now  ships sailed and there are good things  that have come out of that  so I say embrace it don't root for Fox  to fail root for them to get it right  because let's be honest when they get it  right they get it really right they just  need to work on t